I have just ascended a Tourist, after many weeks of trying. It is by far the
most difficult character I've played. This is the sixth class I ascend with,
after Elf, Wizard, Barbarian, Healer and Priest, hence this braggard post
(there are twelve classes in all). Has anybody ascended all classes yet?

What made this character ascendable was the combination of a cursed magic
lamp, a lawful altar and many fountains to dilute useless potions with.
When a wand of wishing was found somewhere near level 20, this tourist's
armor class zoomed down to the -30's, and after the castle WOW, an unbeatable
combination of +6 blessed rustproof Stormy, and -45 AC (all rustproof), all
useful intrinsics and 130 HP made it an easy cruise to ascension. The only
scare came when, while cleaning out a throne room, it turned out that an
"@" was in fact Medusa herself, right in the middle of a room full of nasties.
If it weren't for an amulet of life saving, this tourist would be yet another
statue... This really took me by surprise. I thought Medusa was always in
a room by herself (with perhaps a couple of random monsters), but not in
a "special" room! On that particular level, only a few statues were to be
found, not especially many more than usual, and I had no inkling this was
THE Medusa level until it was too late (well, almost too late; thank the
Nethack gods for amulets of life saving!).
Something else that made the game easy: three beehives encountered in all!

Well, back to work now. Keep nethacking!

